  "analyst_notes": "Following Carvana's Q3 2026 beat on October 28, 2026 (217,385 retail units, $800M Adjusted EBITDA), BofA, Barclays, Citizens JMP, and UBS raised targets into the $81-$85 range, while Needham ($120 to $100) and BTIG ($87 to $82) trimmed targets on macro and interest-rate caution. The ~6.3 pp gap between the Street's ~13.8% implied upside and our +7.4% base case reflects a ~2.1x higher implied P/E (38.1x vs. 36x) or ~6% higher FY2027 EPS ($2.29 vs. $2.16). Stifel's November 17, 2026 initiation ($85, Buy) occurred after the November 13 reference close and is excluded.",
